    "descriptions": [
      {
        "lang": "en",
        "description": "A histologically validated probabilistic atlas of seven REM-related nuclei in the human brainstem, in MNI152 space (0.5 mm isotropic), built from 10 ex vivo 7-tesla MRI specimens (78.1 micron isotropic). Each nucleus was manually delineated on high-resolution ex vivo MRI, spatially normalised to MNI152 space, averaged voxel-wise across specimens to give a probabilistic map, and thresholded at probability &gt;= 0.3 to give a binary atlas. For 12 ROIs (DR, PAG, and right/left PTg, LDTg, LDTgV, LC, SubC), both probabilistic (_prob, voxel values 0-1) and binary (_bin_thr30, threshold 0.3) NIfTI files are provided, together with README and LICENSE. Licensed under CC BY-NC-ND 4.0.",
        "descriptionType": "Abstract"
      }
    ],
